blurb = "Depicts workers scraping rock tripe off a cliff face, while suspended in baskets above a gorge.

Although rock tripe is called iwatake (\"rock mushroom\") in Japanese, it is actually an edible lichen (Umbilicaria esculenta) that grows on sheer, exposed mountain cliffs. Although considered at best a starvation food in most of the world, Japanese cuisine appreciates its elastic texture and earthy flavor. It requires extensive processing by repeated boiling to reduce bitterness, and is sometimes prepared with sugar and soy sauce or baked into cakes."
